artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $p$ be a prime number and let $\mathbb{Q}_p$ denote the field of $p$-adic numbers, equipped with the $p$-adic valuation $v_p$. Consider the following two infinite totally ramified algebraic extensions of $\mathbb{Q}_p$:
\begin{itemize}
\item $K_1 = \mathbb{Q}_p(\zeta_{p^\infty})$, obtained by adjoining a compatible system of primitive $p^n$-th roots of unity $\zeta_{p^n}$ for all $n \geq 1$;
\item $K_2 = \mathbb{Q}_p(p^{1/p^\infty})$, obtained by adjoining a compatible system of $p^n$-th roots of $p$ for all $n \geq 1$.
\end{itemize}
Each $K_i$ is regarded as a valued field with the unique extension of $v_p$. Recall that a valued field $(K,v)$ is called Kaplansky (i.e., satisfies Kaplansky's hypothesis (A)) if its residue characteristic $p$ satisfies: the value group is $p$-divisible, the residue field is perfect, and the residue field admits no finite separable extension whose degree is divisible by $p$. Recall further that a maximal immediate extension of $(K,v)$ is an extension with the same value group and residue field that admits no proper immediate extension, and that a henselian valued field of residue characteristic $p>0$ is called tame if it is algebraically maximal, its value group is $p$-divisible, and its residue field is perfect.

Neither $K_1$ nor $K_2$ is a Kaplansky field, and consequently each admits uncountably many pairwise non-isomorphic maximal immediate extensions, realising uncountably many distinct elementary theories in the language $L_{\mathrm{val}}$ of valued fields, of which uncountably many are undecidable. Among these maximal immediate extensions, those whose elementary $L_{\mathrm{val}}$-theory is decidable are known to be tame valued fields.

Problem. Describe the internal valuation-theoretic and algebraic structure of the maximal immediate extensions of $(K_i, v_p)$ for $i = 1, 2$, beyond the mere cardinality statement that there are infinitely (in fact uncountably) many. In particular, identify intrinsic structural invariants or properties of such a maximal immediate extension that characterise when its elementary $L_{\mathrm{val}}$-theory is decidable versus undecidable.

